L wrote:
> Okay: boomerangs exist, but nobody uses them because they're designed
> to be thrown once, but don't do enough damage in a single throw to
> justify keeping them.
> 
> So, I thought that a magical boomerang that returned to the player once
> it strikes an enemy or an obstacle would give the player more incentive
> to play with them and their unique attack range.
> 
> http://www.greyfire.org/~l/magicb.diff
> 
> Magic boomerangs are not randomly generated. Using a scroll of enchant
> armor on a wooden boomerang changes it to a magic boomerang, which is
> identical except that it teleports back to the player's hand after it
> hits something.
> 
> Also, eating a magic boomerang confers teleport control.
> 

I really like this patch; I was just thinking the other day how 
boomerangs are cool but useless.

I would like to see them improved in a different way. Let boomerangs be 
like daggers; stackable and you can throw more than one with enough 
skill. They would also have to be generated more frequently; a boomerang 
trap would be pretty cool. Let them have a chance of breaking when 
hitting a wall, if some balance is needed here.

Then boomerangs would be better than daggers in an open area at close 
ranges, but daggers would be more useful in the far more common narrow 
spaces and long ranges.


